# Headers Cloudflare Pages applies to what it serves.
#
# The site had none. It is a static site that handles people's documents, and
# a policy is the cheapest hardening there is: it does not stop a bug in our
# code, it stops a bug in our code from being useful to somebody else.
#
# Two honest limits, written down so nobody assumes more than is here.
#
# script-src carries 'unsafe-inline'. Next puts its hydration data in inline
# script tags, and the usual answer, a nonce, needs a server to generate one
# per request. This is a static export with no server, so the choice is
# 'unsafe-inline' or no policy at all. What remains is still worth having:
# scripts cannot be loaded from another origin, which is how injected code
# normally arrives.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is required, not optional. HEIC decoding, OCR and PDF
# rendering are WebAssembly, and without it they do not run at all.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://victorfolorunsoofficial--vantly-convert-web.modal.run https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://data.iana.org; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# The two OCR pages, and only those, may load a script from the CDN that
# serves Tesseract. Its worker and language data are fetched at runtime, and
# the worker arrives as a script rather than as data, so connect-src is not
# enough on its own.
#
# Nothing here needs 'unsafe-eval'. That was assumed from reading library
# source and it was wrong: Terser minifies quite happily under the strict
# policy, tested on the built site before this was written.
/image-to-text/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/pdf-ocr/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The domain tools ask each ending's own registry, and there are hundreds of
# them at addresses IANA publishes rather than ones we could list here. So
# connect-src has to allow https on these two pages. Everything else stays
# shut, which is the difference between a wide hole and a wide site.
/domain-name-checker/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/domain-name-generator/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Song to tonic solfa talks to its transcription service, and plays the song
# and the piano track straight from it, so these pages need connect-src and
# media-src for that origin: the Modal app in solfaflow's prototype/modal_app.py.
# Change both here if NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLFA_URL ever points somewhere else.
#
# The ! line detaches the site-wide policy first. Cloudflare joins two copies
# of a header with a comma, and two policies are both enforced, so without it
# the stricter one above would still block the audio.
/song-to-tonic-solfa/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://victorfolorunsoofficial--solfaflow-web.us-east.modal.run; media-src 'self' blob: https://victorfolorunsoofficial--solfaflow-web.us-east.modal.run; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Everything under _next is content addressed: the filename changes when the
# file does, so it can be cached forever without ever going stale.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
